The task is complete. Here's the summary.

**Outcome**
Implemented the G03 converter that turns selected, redacted failure traces into re-runnable eval samples, in all 7 target-scope files.

**Deliverables** (all new; no pre-existing file modified or deleted)
- `scripts/lib/trace-to-eval-sample.mjs` — pure, explicitly triggered converter. `traceToEvalSample(trace)` → `{ok,sample}` / `{ok:false,diagnostics}`; `traceToEvalSamples(traces)` → batch with per-trace `rejected` diagnostics. Samples carry `expected{before-fix,after-fix}`, bounded `reproducer{kind ∈ scenario|route|command-id, ref}`, `selector{runId,attempt}`, and a deterministic 16-hex digest. Non-redacted traces (raw prompt/messages/body/authorization/apiKey/headers incl. nested, or `sk-`/`phc_`/`ghp_`/`github_pat_`/`AKIA`/`ASIA`/`xox`/`Bearer`/private-key) are refused whole (`trace-not-redacted`). No scheduler/daemon.
- `scripts/lib/trace-to-eval-sample.d.mts` — declaration surface.
- `tests/unit/trace-to-eval-sample.test.ts` — 7 focused tests.
- `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-trace-to-eval-sample.md`, `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/g03-trace-to-eval-sample.md`, `g03-acceptance.json`, `G03-SHA256SUMS`.

